# OduSphere ownership manifest — the machine-readable boundary between the
# upstream-owned CORE (read-only for the sphere and its agent) and the
# SPHERE-owned lane (writable). Human documentation: .docs/ownership.md.
#
# Consumed by the OduSphere CLI to build the agent-container mount plan and the
# deploy-time core-integrity gate.
#
# Format: one `<mode> <path>` per line; `mode` is `rw` or `ro`; `path` is a
# DIRECTORY relative to the repo root (directories only — single-file bind
# mounts break on git's rename-replace). A deeper path overrides its parent.
# Every path not covered by an `rw` line is core: read-only for the agent and
# verified byte-for-byte against the upstream template at deploy time.
# `.git/` is not listed — the CLI always mounts it rw (the agent must be able
# to commit and push).

rw sphere/
rw .claude/skills/
ro .claude/skills/odu-doc-i18n/
